# Task Routing

The seven `rd-*` document skills can be used independently and in any order. They are not a forced pipeline.

## Available Skills

| Skill | Deliverable | Daily work |
|---|---|---|
| `$rd-requirement` | Structured requirements / PRD / SRS | Requirements analysis and product/design input |
| `$rd-feasibility` | Feasibility study / feasibility analysis report | Project feasibility and decision support |
| `$rd-research` | Evidence package / source notes | Literature, standards, policy, vendor, market, and technical evidence for downstream documents |
| `$rd-solution` | Technical proposal / high-level design / construction plan | System architecture and solution documentation |
| `$rd-design` | Detailed design document | Interface, data, flow, error, security, and concurrency design |
| `$rd-specification` | Standards/specification draft or clause review | Standards formulation, revision, and clause-level review |
| `$rd-review` | Document review findings | Requirements, feasibility, proposal, design, and standards review |

## Authoring To Review Mapping

| Authoring skill | Review skill | Review mode |
|---|---|---|
| `$rd-requirement` to PRD / SRS | `$rd-review` | Requirements Review |
| `$rd-feasibility` to feasibility report | `$rd-review` | Feasibility Review |
| `$rd-solution` to proposal / high-level design / construction plan | `$rd-review` | Proposal Review |
| `$rd-design` to detailed design | `$rd-review` | Design Review |
| `$rd-specification` to standard / specification / clause draft | `$rd-review` | Standards Review |

`$rd-research` is not part of the authoring-to-review chain. Use it as evidence input for `$rd-feasibility`, `$rd-solution`, `$rd-specification`, `$rd-design`, or fact-dependent `$rd-review`.

## Invocation Guidance

- Invoke the relevant skill by name when the task clearly matches it.
- Do not force a full PRD-to-design pipeline for small tasks.
- For reviews, lead with severity-graded findings.
- For standards work, cite exact clauses and mark missing evidence as requiring human verification.
- For feasibility work, separate facts, assumptions, estimates, and unknowns.
- Use `$rd-research` when external evidence materially affects a feasibility, solution, standards, design, or review conclusion.

## Parallel Work

Use parallel or background work only when subtasks are independent, write scopes do not overlap, and the outputs can be merged without ambiguity.
